The full arbitrary-list theorem now closes: the base proof establishes membership and the loop invariant, and the second definition composes that proved invariant into the function call. I’m doing the final gate now—bounded symbolic claims, wrong-result mutation, exact source/translation consistency, a clean `prove.sh`, then one end-to-end rerun.
